#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:1
msgid ""
"Masterclass 22.10: Hamiltonian replica exchange with PLUMED and GROMACS"
msgstr "Masterclass 22.10：PLUMED と GROMACS による Hamiltonian Replica Exchange"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:3
msgid "Origin"
msgstr "作成について"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:5
msgid "This masterclass was authored by Giovanni Bussi on June 21, 2022"
msgstr "この Masterclass は、2022年6月21日に Giovanni Bussi によって作成された。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:7
msgid "Aims"
msgstr "目的"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:9
msgid ""
"In this Masterclass, we will discuss how to run Hamiltonian replica exchange"
" using PLUMED and GROMACS. We will also understand how to analyze the "
"resulting trajectories. It is highly recommended to follow "
"[this](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-doc/html/masterclass-21-5.html) "
"masterclass in advance."
msgstr ""
"この Masterclass では、PLUMED と GROMACS による Hamiltonian Replica Exchange "
"の実行と、得られた Trajectories の解析を学ぶ。先に[こちら](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/masterclass-21-5.html)の Masterclass を終えることを強く勧める。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:12
msgid "Objectives"
msgstr "到達目標"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:14
msgid "Once you have completed this Masterclass you will be able to:"
msgstr "この Masterclass を終えると、次のことができるようになる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:16
msgid ""
"Use PLUMED to manipulate GROMACS topologies and prepare a solute tempering "
"simulation."
msgstr "PLUMED で GROMACS Topologies を操作し、Solute Tempering を準備する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:17
msgid ""
"Use PLUMED and GROMACS to run replica-exchange simulations with multiple "
"topologies."
msgstr "異なる Topologies を持つ Replica Exchange を、PLUMED と GROMACS で実行する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:18
msgid ""
"Use WHAM to combine multiple simulations performed with different topologies"
" and/or bias potentials."
msgstr "異なる Topologies や BiasPotentials で実行した計算を、WHAM で統合する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:20
msgid "Setting up PLUMED"
msgstr "PLUMED のセットアップ"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:22
msgid ""
"For this masterclass you will need versions of PLUMED and GROMACS that are "
"compiled using the MPI library. In order to obtain the correct versions, "
"please follow the instructions at [this "
"link](https://github.com/plumed/masterclass-2022)."
msgstr ""
"MPI ライブラリでコンパイルした PLUMED と GROMACS "
"が必要である。適切な版の導入は、[こちら](https://github.com/plumed/masterclass-2022)の手順に従う。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:25
msgid "Resources"
msgstr "資料"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:27
msgid ""
"The data needed to execute the exercises of this Masterclass can be found on"
" [GitHub](https://github.com/plumed/masterclass-22-10). You can clone this "
"repository locally on your machine using the following command:"
msgstr ""
"演習に必要なデータは [GitHub](https://github.com/plumed/masterclass-22-10) "
"にある。次のコマンドでリポジトリを手元に clone できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:35
msgid ""
"**All the exercises were tested with PLUMED version 2.8.0 and GROMACS "
"2020.6**"
msgstr "**すべての演習は PLUMED 2.8.0 と GROMACS 2020.6 で動作確認されている。**"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:37
msgid ""
"Additional documentation about the replica exchange implementation discussed"
" in this Masterclass can be found at [this page](https://www.plumed.org/doc-"
"master/user-doc/html/hrex.html)."
msgstr ""
"この実装の追加説明は、[こちら](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/hrex.html)にある。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:39
msgid "Exercises"
msgstr "演習"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:41
msgid ""
"Throughout this Masterclass we will run simulations of **alanine dipeptide "
"in water** using GROMACS and PLUMED. Whereas this system is too simple to be"
" considered a proper benchmark for enhanced sampling methods, it is complex "
"enough to be used for learning about them. This Masterclass regards a "
"specific implementation of Hamiltonian replica exchange that is only "
"available when combining GROMACS and PLUMED."
msgstr ""
"全体を通して、GROMACS と PLUMED で**水中の Alanine Dipeptide** を計算する。本格的な Enhanced "
"Sampling の Benchmark には単純すぎるが、学習には十分な複雑さを持つ。この Masterclass は、GROMACS と "
"PLUMED を組み合わせた場合にのみ利用できる、特定の Hamiltonian Replica Exchange の実装を扱う。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:46
msgid ""
"Notice that simulations might take up to a couple of hours, depending on the"
" hardware you have access to. The version of GROMACS that we provide on our "
"conda channel is not optimized. Compiling GROMACS directly on your machine "
"might lead to much better performance. In addition, using a GPU will also "
"make your simulations significantly faster."
msgstr ""
"ハードウェアによっては、数時間かかる。配布する conda Channel の GROMACS "
"は最適化されていないため、自分のマシンでコンパイルすると大幅に速くなる場合がある。GPU の利用も高速化に役立つ。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:51
msgid "Introduction to Hamiltonian replica exchange"
msgstr "Hamiltonian Replica Exchange の入門"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:53
msgid ""
"In [masterclass-21-5](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/masterclass-21-5.html) we learned how to run replica-exchange "
"simulations where each replica was possibly feeling different biasing "
"forces. A typical example is umbrella sampling with replica exchange, where "
"each replica has a restraint located in a different position. Another "
"example is bias-exchange metadynamics, where each replica is biased along a "
"different collective variable. We have also seen parallel-tempering "
"metadynamics, where replicas are kept at a different temperature and, at the"
" same time, keep track of different history-dependent potentials. All these "
"examples are a form of Hamiltonian replica exchange, since different "
"replicas are subject to different potential energy functions, and thus "
"different Hamiltonians."
msgstr ""
"[masterclass-21-5](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/masterclass-21-5.html) では、各 Replica に異なる Biasing Forces を加える "
"Replica Exchange を学んだ。典型例は、異なる位置の Restraint を使う Umbrella Sampling と Replica "
"Exchange の組み合わせである。他にも、各 Replica の異なる CV に Bias を加える Bias-Exchange "
"Metadynamics がある。異なる温度と、それぞれの History-dependent Potential を用いる Parallel-"
"Tempering Metadynamics も扱った。どれも Replicas の Potential Energy Functions、すなわち "
"Hamiltonians が異なるため、Hamiltonian Replica Exchange の一種である。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:63
msgid ""
"In this masterclass we will consider a conceptually similar but technically "
"different implementation of Hamiltonian replica exchange. Here, the "
"different replicas will be simulated using different force field parameters."
" For most of the exercise, we will thus use an empty `plumed.dat` file (no "
"bias added!). You will however need to include this file to ensure PLUMED "
"can be enabled. We will also spend some time in learning how to edit the "
"GROMACS topologies, so as to generate the modified force fields."
msgstr ""
"今回は、概念的には似ているが、技術的には別の実装を扱う。各 Replica を異なる Force Field Parameters "
"で計算する。このため演習の大半では、Bias を加えない空の `plumed.dat` を使う。ただし、PLUMED "
"を有効にするためファイル自体は必要である。変更した Force Fields を作るため、GROMACS Topologies の編集方法も学ぶ。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:69
msgid ""
"In order to use multiple-replica methods, you should run your simulation "
"using MPI. This can be done prefixing your command with `mpiexec -np N "
"--oversubscribe`, where `N` is the number of processes that you want to use "
"and the `--oversubscribe` option is an OpenMPI option that is required to "
"use more processes than the number of available processors. This is "
"typically suboptimal, but we will need it in our lectures to run, e.g., "
"simulations with 16 replicas even if we have a computer with 4 cores."
msgstr ""
"Multi-replica 法は MPI で実行する。コマンドの前に `mpiexec -np N --oversubscribe` を付け、`N` に"
" Process 数を指定する。`--oversubscribe` は、利用できる Processor 数より多くの Processes を使うための "
"OpenMPI のオプションである。通常は最適ではないが、4 Cores のマシンで16 Replicas を実行する場合など、講義では必要になる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:74
msgid ""
"In brief, to run a GROMACS simulation where the individual replicas are in "
"directories names `dir0`, `dir1`, etc and the (possibly empty) `plumed.dat` "
"file is in the parent directory you will need a command such as"
msgstr ""
"例えば、各 Replica のディレクトリを `dir0`、`dir1` などとし、親ディレクトリに、空でもよい `plumed.dat` "
"を置く場合、次のようなコマンドを使う。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:81
msgid ""
"The option `-replex 200` enables replica exchange and ensures exchanges are "
"attempted every 200 steps. The option `-hrex` is specific for the "
"implemenation discussed in this Masterclass, and informs GROMACS and PLUMED "
"that there might be different force fields used in different replicas."
msgstr ""
"`-replex 200` は Replica Exchange を有効にし、200ステップごとに交換を試行する。`-hrex` "
"は今回の実装に固有であり、Replicas 間で Force Fields が異なる可能性を GROMACS と PLUMED に伝える。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:86
msgid ""
"*If you forget the `-hrex` flag, no error will be issued, but the acceptance"
" for exchanges will be incorrectly calculated.*"
msgstr "*`-hrex` を忘れてもエラーは出ないが、交換の Acceptance が誤って計算される。*"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:88
msgid ""
"If you have random crashes on MacOS, try to set this environemnt variable:"
msgstr "macOS で不規則に Crash する場合は、次の環境変数を設定してみる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:94
msgid ""
"In the root directory of this Masterclass you will find a `conf.gro` file, "
"that can be used as a starting configuration for your simulations, a "
"`topol.top` file, which contains the topology information, and a "
"`grompp.mdp` file with reasonable simulation parameters. You have also a "
"`ala.pdb` file, that is basically the `conf.gro` file converted to PDB "
"format, and can be used for the [MOLINFO](https://www.plumed.org/doc-"
"master/user-doc/html/_m_o_l_i_n_f_o.html) action so as to facilitate atom "
"selections in analysis."
msgstr ""
"ルートディレクトリには、初期 Configuration の `conf.gro`、Topology の `topol.top`、妥当な計算パラメータの"
" `grompp.mdp` がある。また、`conf.gro` を PDB に変換した `ala.pdb` は、解析時の原子選択を簡単にする "
"[MOLINFO](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/_m_o_l_i_n_f_o.html) で使える。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:99
msgid "Exercise 1a: Test with different temperatures"
msgstr "演習1a：異なる温度で試す"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:101
msgid ""
"Before swithing to solute tempering, we will play a bit with parallel "
"tempering. Parallel tempering simulations require the highest replica to be "
"hot enough for important energy barriers to be crossed in the simulation. We"
" will first estimate how much we should raise the temperature so as to see "
"forward and backward transitions between the two metastable states of our "
"system."
msgstr ""
"Solute Tempering の前に Parallel Tempering を試す。重要な Energy Barriers "
"を計算中に越えられるよう、最高温度の Replica を十分に高温にする必要がある。まず、2つの Metastable States "
"の往復遷移を見るために、どこまで温度を上げる必要があるかを見積もる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:106
msgid "To do so:"
msgstr "次のように進める。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:107
msgid ""
"Prepare an array of simulations, with temperatures equal to 300, 400, 500, "
"600, 700, 800, 900, 1000"
msgstr "温度を300、400、500、600、700、800、900、1000とする一連の計算を準備する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:108
msgid ""
"Run each of them for 1 ns and check at which temperature you have at least "
"one transition from the initial basin to the other one and one backward "
"transition"
msgstr "各温度で1 ns 計算し、初期 Basin からもう一方への遷移と、戻る遷移が少なくとも1回ずつ起きる温度を調べる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:110
msgid "These are serial simulations, so you can run them with this command:"
msgstr "これらは Serial 計算なので、次のコマンドで実行できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:119
msgid "though it is recommended to use a script to run your simulations."
msgstr "ただし、複数の計算はスクリプトで実行することを勧める。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:121
msgid ""
"To analyze the resulting trajectories you can use PLUMED "
"[driver](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-doc/html/driver.html)"
msgstr ""
"解析には PLUMED の [driver](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/driver.html) を使える。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:125
msgid "with the following `plumed.dat` file:"
msgstr "次の `plumed.dat` を使う。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:133
msgid ""
"You can then plot the second column of the resulting `COLVAR` file and see "
"if there is a transition from the first basin (phi in range (-3,-1)) to the "
"second basin (phi in range (0.5,1.5)), and back. Answer the following "
"question:"
msgstr ""
"出力 `COLVAR` の2列目を描き、最初の Basin（phi が -3～-1）から、2つ目（phi "
"が0.5～1.5）への遷移と、その逆を確認する。次の問いに答えてほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:136
msgid ""
"How much should you increase the temperature to see a transition back-and-"
"forth between the two basins?"
msgstr "2つの Basins 間の往復遷移を見るには、どこまで温度を上げる必要があるだろうか。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:138
msgid ""
"The result will depend on stochastic factors, but also on the length of the "
"simulation. I recommend running a 1 ns long simulation (500000 steps), but "
"you can try with a longer or shorter trajectory."
msgstr "結果は確率的な要因だけでなく、計算時間にも依存する。1 ns、500000ステップを勧めるが、長くしたり短くしたりしてもよい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:141
msgid "Exercise 1b: Run a parallel tempering simulation"
msgstr "演習1b：Parallel Tempering の実行"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:143
msgid ""
"Once you have identified this temperature, you can run a parallel tempering "
"simulation. You will need a number of replicas to bridge from T=300 to the "
"temperature you have identified. As a first guess, you can place them in a "
"geometric series (that's the allocation that leads to uniform acceptance in "
"a system with temperature-independent specific heat)."
msgstr ""
"必要な温度が分かったら、Parallel Tempering を行う。T=300からその温度をつなぐ Replicas が必要である。最初は "
"Geometric Series で配置するとよい。Heat Capacity が温度に依存しない系では、これが一様な Acceptance を与える。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:147
msgid ""
"Let's say that you want to try with 16 replicas. You should create 16 "
"directories named `dir0`, `dir1`, ... `dir15` and place a file named "
"`topol.tpr` in each. Each `topol.tpr` files will be created setting a "
"different temperature in the `grompp.mdp` file. We will not need PLUMED for "
"this exercise, so the simulation can be run with a command like this one:"
msgstr ""
"16 Replicas を試すとする。`dir0`、`dir1`、…、`dir15` の16ディレクトリを作り、それぞれに `topol.tpr` "
"を置く。各 `topol.tpr` は、`grompp.mdp` の温度を変えて生成する。この演習に PLUMED は不要であり、次のように実行できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:156
msgid ""
"The `-replex` option tells to GROMACS how frequently exchanges should be "
"attempted. The average acceptance will be reported at the end of the "
"`md.log` file."
msgstr "`-replex` で交換の試行頻度を指定する。平均 Acceptance は `md.log` の末尾に出力される。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:159
msgid ""
"The hottest replica will display transitions between the two metastable "
"states. Thanks to the exchanges, both states will be observed also in the "
"replica that is kept as T=300K."
msgstr ""
"最高温度の Replica では、2つの Metastable States 間の遷移が起きる。交換によって、T=300 K の Replica "
"でも両状態を観測できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:161 INSTRUCTIONS.md:279
msgid "Now answer the following questions:"
msgstr "次の問いに答えてほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:162
msgid ""
"How many replicas do you need to have an acceptance that is at least 30%? "
"(the answer will depend on the maximum temperature you have chosen)"
msgstr "Acceptance を30%以上にするには、いくつの Replicas が必要だろうか。答えは選んだ最高温度に依存する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:163
msgid ""
"How much is the relative population of the two metastable states at T=300? "
"Plot this population as a function of the temperature (you can just extract "
"results from the different replicas)."
msgstr "T=300における2状態の相対的な Population はどの程度か。各 Replica の結果から、温度の関数として描いてほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:165
msgid "Exercise 2a: Setting up scaled Hamiltonians"
msgstr "演習2a：Scaling した Hamiltonians の準備"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:167
msgid ""
"In order to run Hamiltonian replica exchange simulations with multiple "
"topologies, we will have first to learn how to generate the multiple "
"topologies. Different tools could be used (including editing the `topol.top`"
" file by hand!) but we will now learn how to use the "
"[partial_tempering](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/partial_tempering.html) tool available in PLUMED. This tool "
"basically allows you to generate topologies where the energy of a subset of "
"the atom have be scaled by a chosen factor. Remember that dividing the "
"energy by a factor 2 is equivalent to multiplying the temperature by a "
"factor 2."
msgstr ""
"異なる Topologies の Hamiltonian Replica Exchange を行うには、まず Topologies "
"の生成方法を学ぶ。`topol.top` を手で編集するなどの方法もあるが、ここでは PLUMED の "
"[partial_tempering](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/partial_tempering.html) を使う。選択した原子群の Energy を、指定の係数で Scaling した "
"Topologies を作れる。Energy を2で割るのは、温度を2倍することに相当する点を思い出してほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:172
msgid ""
"Let's first have a look at the `topol.top` file. In this file there are a "
"number of lines that look like `#include ...`, so that this file is not "
"self-contained. The first thing that we have to do is to generate a self-"
"contained topology file:"
msgstr ""
"まず `topol.top` を見る。`#include ...` のような行が多く、これだけでは完結していない。最初に、自己完結した Topology"
" を作る。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:179
msgid ""
"Have a look at the resulting `processed.top` file with a text editor. This "
"file does not contain only information about alanine dipeptide, but also "
"about the generic force-field parameters. It is thus self-contained."
msgstr ""
"`processed.top` を Text Editor で確認する。Alanine Dipeptide の情報だけでなく、汎用の Force "
"Field Parameters も含むため、このファイルだけで完結する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:183
msgid ""
"Then you should edit the `processed.top` file to indicate which atoms you "
"want to scale. To do so you have to add an underscore (`_`) to the atom name"
" of the selected atoms. For instance, this line:"
msgstr ""
"次に `processed.top` を編集し、Scaling する原子を指定する。選択した原子の名前に "
"Underscore（`_`）を付ける。例えば、次の行は、"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:188
msgid "should be modified to this line:"
msgstr "次のように変更する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:192
msgid ""
"To perform a solute tempering simulation, you should add the underscore to "
"all the solute atoms (look in the `[ atoms ]` section). Once this is done "
"you can use the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Solute Tempering では、すべての Solute Atoms に Underscore を付ける。`[ atoms ]` "
"を確認してほしい。その後、次を実行する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:196
msgid ""
"This will scale the Hamiltonian of the selected atoms by a factor 1.0 (which"
" means: no change!). Have a look at the resulting `scaled.top` file and find"
" out what has changed. You can also try to apply two different scaling "
"factors and check the difference:"
msgstr ""
"選んだ原子の Hamiltonian を係数1.0、つまり変更なしで Scaling する。`scaled.top` "
"で何が変わったかを確認する。他の2つの係数も試し、違いを比べられる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:204
msgid "Exercise 2b: Sanity check on generated topologies"
msgstr "演習2b：生成した Topologies の妥当性確認"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:206
msgid ""
"Notice that these scaled topologies can be used to run GROMACS simulations. "
"The `parial_tempering` script is far from perfect. We will now make some "
"sanity check. To do these checks, we will either generate a new trajectory "
"or simply take one of the trajectories that we generated in the previous "
"exercise. We will then used a GROMACS tool named `rerun`, which allows "
"recomputing the energy along a trajectory using a new topology."
msgstr ""
"生成した Topologies は GROMACS で使えるが、`parial_tempering` "
"は完全ではないため、妥当性を確認する。新しく計算した、または以前の演習の Trajectory を使う。GROMACS の `rerun` は、新しい "
"Topology で Trajectory の Energy を再計算できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:208
msgid "First, create an energy file corresponding to the original topology:"
msgstr "まず、元の Topology の Energy ファイルを作る。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:214
msgid ""
"The resulting `ener.edr` file can be converted to a text file with the "
"`gmx_mpi energy` command."
msgstr "`ener.edr` は、`gmx_mpi energy` でテキストに変換できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:216
msgid ""
"Then, generate a new topology with scaling factor 1.0 and compute energies "
"again:"
msgstr "次に、係数1.0で新しい Topology を作り、再度 Energy を計算する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:223
msgid "The resulting energies should be identical!"
msgstr "Energy は一致するはずである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:225
msgid ""
"As a second check, generate a new topology where you scaled *all* atoms "
"(make sure to also select water!) by a factor 0.5:"
msgstr "2つ目の確認では、水も含めた*すべて*の原子を、係数0.5で Scaling する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:233
msgid ""
"This time, dihedral angles, LJ, and Coulomb energies should be multiplied by"
" 0.5."
msgstr "この場合、Dihedral、LJ、Coulomb の Energies は0.5倍になるはずである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:235
msgid ""
"This is a very important check. The `partial_tempering` script is not "
"compatible with some specific functional forms, e.g., CHARMM CMAP (search "
"PLUMED mailing list for a fix). In case you are using an incompatible force "
"field, you will find inconsistencies in these sanity checks. For the "
"provided `topol.top` file, everything should work."
msgstr ""
"これは非常に重要な確認である。`partial_tempering` は、CHARMM CMAP など一部の関数形式に対応していない。修正方法は "
"PLUMED Mailing List で探せる。非対応の Force Field では、この確認で不一致が見つかる。付属の `topol.top` "
"では、正常に動くはずである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:242
msgid "Exercise 2c: Sanity check on replica-exchange implementation"
msgstr "演習2c：Replica Exchange 実装の妥当性確認"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:244
msgid ""
"Another thing that we will have to check now is if acceptance is computed "
"correctly. The code inserted in GROMACS to implement this calculation is non"
" trivial and quite fragile. To do this check, you should run a short "
"Hamiltonian replica exchange with two equivalent topology files. For "
"instance, you can use the original `topol.tpr` file and the one that you "
"obtained with scaling factor 1.0. Make sure that the two tpr files are using"
" a different seed for randomizing the initial velocities or, even better, "
"use two different `conf.gro` files to initialize the two simulations. For "
"everything else, use the same settings you will use in production (ideally, "
"same number of processes per replica, same GPU settings, etc)."
msgstr ""
"Acceptance が正しく計算されるかも確認する。このために GROMACS に加えたコードは単純ではなく、壊れやすい部分がある。元の "
"`topol.tpr` と係数1.0のものなど、等価な2つの Topologies で短い Hamiltonian Replica Exchange "
"を行う。初期速度の Seed を変え、できれば異なる `conf.gro` から始める。他の条件は本計算と同じにし、Replica 当たりの "
"Process 数や GPU の設定もそろえるのが望ましい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:250
msgid "Now run a short replica exchange simulation:"
msgstr "短い Replica Exchange を実行する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:255
msgid ""
"As written above, `plumed.dat` can be just an empty file. Check the "
"resulting acceptance. Since the Hamiltonians are identical, the acceptance "
"**should be exactly 1.0**."
msgstr ""
"前述のとおり、`plumed.dat` は空でよい。Hamiltonians が同じなので、Acceptance "
"は**厳密に1.0になるはず**である。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:258
msgid ""
"Notice that whereas this is formally true there might be numerical issues "
"that make this test fail. Specifically:"
msgstr "形式上はそうなるが、数値上の問題で確認に失敗する場合がある。具体例を示す。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:261
msgid "Dynamic load balancing (can be switched off with `mdrun -dlb no`)"
msgstr "Dynamic Load Balancing。`mdrun -dlb no` で無効にできる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:262
msgid ""
"When using GPUs or a large number of MPI processes, GROMACS might also "
"optimize the PME calculation dynamically, altering the acceptacte in this "
"case (can be switched off with `mdrun -notunepme`)."
msgstr ""
"GPU や多数の MPI Processes を使うと、GROMACS が PME を動的に最適化し、この場合の Acceptance "
"を変える可能性がある。`mdrun -notunepme` で無効にできる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:264
msgid ""
"See also [here](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/issues/1177) on GitHub for"
" a discussion of this issue."
msgstr ""
"この問題の議論は、GitHub "
"の[こちら](https://github.com/plumed/plumed2/issues/1177)も参照してほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:266
msgid "Exercise 2d: Find minimum scaling factor needed to cross the barrier"
msgstr "演習2d：Barrier を越えるための最小 Scaling Factor の特定"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:268
msgid ""
"You are now able to generate tpr files where the energy of a subset of the "
"atoms is scaled. We will do something similar to exercise 1a above, but "
"playing with scaling factor instead of temperature. Make sure that you "
"select all (and only) the atoms belonging to the solute (alanine dipeptide),"
" so as to implement solute tempering. Try to run a set of 1 ns long "
"simulations, with scaling factors decreasing (e.g., 1.0, 0.9, 0.8, etc). Now"
" answer the following question:"
msgstr ""
"原子群の Energy を Scaling した tpr を生成できるようになった。演習1aと同様に、今度は温度の代わりに Scaling Factor"
" を変える。Solute Tempering のため、Solute の Alanine Dipeptide "
"に属する原子を、すべて、かつそれだけを選ぶ。係数を1.0、0.9、0.8などと下げて1 ns ずつ計算し、次の問いに答えてほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:271
msgid ""
"How much should you decrease the scaling factor to see transitions between "
"the two metastable states in the first nanosecond?"
msgstr "最初の1 ns で2つの Metastable States 間の遷移を見るには、係数をどこまで下げる必要があるだろうか。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:274
msgid "Exercise 3: Run Hamiltonian replica exchange simulations"
msgstr "演習3：Hamiltonian Replica Exchange の実行"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:276
msgid ""
"Now run a Hamiltonian replica exchange simulation with multiple replicas, "
"bridging from lambda=1.0 to the minimun value identified in the previous "
"point. I would suggest using a linear distribution in lambda rather than a "
"geometric one, but you can experiment. Similarly to parallel tempering, we "
"can for now just analyze the reference replica (at lambda=1.0)."
msgstr ""
"lambda=1.0から前の最小値をつなぐ、複数の Replicas で計算する。lambda は Geometric "
"でなく線形の配置を勧めるが、他も試してよい。Parallel Tempering と同様に、まずは lambda=1.0 の Reference "
"Replica だけを解析する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:280
msgid ""
"How many replicas (and which is the optimal distribution) you need to have "
"an acceptance that is at least 30%? (the answer will depend on the minimum "
"lambda you have chosen). Is this smaller or larger than the number of "
"replicas that you used for exercise 1b above?"
msgstr ""
"Acceptance を30%以上にするには、Replicas はいくつ必要で、どの配置が最適だろうか。選んだ最小 lambda "
"に依存する。演習1bより Replicas は少ないか、多いか。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:281
msgid ""
"How much is the relative population of the two metastable states at T=300? "
"Plot this population as a function of lambda (you can just extract results "
"from the different replicas). Is there any relationship between the "
"dependence on lambda and the dependence on T that we have seen in exercise "
"1b above?"
msgstr ""
"T=300での2状態の相対的な Population を、各 Replica から取り出して lambda "
"の関数として描く。演習1bの温度依存性とは、何か関係があるだろうか。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:284
msgid "Exercise 4: Analyze Hamiltonian replica exchange simulations with WHAM"
msgstr "演習4：WHAM による Hamiltonian Replica Exchange の解析"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:286
msgid ""
"So far we only analized the reference replica (lambda=1.0). We can however "
"do better and combine all replicas with WHAM. To this aim you should:"
msgstr "ここまでは lambda=1.0 だけを解析したが、WHAM ですべての Replicas を統合できる。次の手順で行う。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:287
msgid ""
"Concatenate all trajectories in a single file (`gmx_mpi trjcat -cat -f "
"dir?/traj_comp.xtc dir??/traj_comp.xtc -o traj_multi.xtc`)."
msgstr ""
"全 Trajectories を1ファイルに連結する（`gmx_mpi trjcat -cat -f dir?/traj_comp.xtc "
"dir??/traj_comp.xtc -o traj_multi.xtc`）。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:288
msgid ""
"Recompute the potential energy according to each of the tpr files (for each "
"replica) (`gmx_mpi mdrun -rerun traj_multi.xtc -s dir0/topol.tpr -e "
"energy0.edr`, `gmx_mpi mdrun -rerun traj_multi.xtc -s dir1/topol.tpr -e "
"ener1.edr`, etc.)."
msgstr ""
"各 Replica の tpr で Potential Energy を再計算する（`gmx_mpi mdrun -rerun "
"traj_multi.xtc -s dir0/topol.tpr -e energy0.edr`、`gmx_mpi mdrun -rerun "
"traj_multi.xtc -s dir1/topol.tpr -e ener1.edr` など）。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:291
msgid ""
"Convert the energies to text files (`echo 11 | gmx_mpi energy -f ener0.edr "
"-xvg no -e energy0.xvg -xvg no`, etc.). 11 should select the potential "
"energy."
msgstr ""
"Energy をテキストに変換する（`echo 11 | gmx_mpi energy -f ener0.edr -xvg no -e "
"energy0.xvg -xvg no` など）。11は Potential Energy を選択するはずである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:295
msgid ""
"Then you can use the provided python wham script to compute the weight of "
"all frames with the following python commands:"
msgstr "付属の Python WHAM スクリプトで、次のようにすべての Frames の Weight を計算する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:319
msgid "Now plot the `weights` array and answer the following questions:"
msgstr "`weights` Array を描き、次に答えてほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:320
msgid ""
"How does the weight depend on the frame index? Remember that the replica "
"exchange trajectories were concatenated. Can you recognize those frames "
"coming from the first, second, etc replica?"
msgstr ""
"Weight は Frame の Index にどう依存するか。Trajectories は連結されている点を思い出してほしい。どの Frames "
"が1番目、2番目などの Replica に由来するかを識別できるだろうか。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:322
msgid ""
"Compute the population of the two states by summing the weight of all states"
" in the two basins."
msgstr "2つの Basins 内の Weight をそれぞれ足し、各状態の Population を求める。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:323
msgid ""
"Modify the script above to compute weights corresponding to replicas other "
"than the first one, and compute the population of the two states as a "
"function of lambda."
msgstr ""
"最初以外の Replicas に対応する Weight を計算するようスクリプトを変え、lambda の関数として2状態の Population "
"を求める。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:326
msgid "Exercise 5: Optimize the lambda ladder"
msgstr "演習5：Lambda Ladder の最適化"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:328
msgid ""
"The aim of this exercise is to optimize the list of values of lambda. As a "
"target, we will try to make the product of the acceptances as large as "
"possible. We will do this *without* running new simulations, i.e. just "
"analyzing the simulation above."
msgstr ""
"lambda の値のリストを最適化する。目標は、Acceptance "
"の積を最大にすることである。新しい計算は*行わず*、これまでのシミュレーションを解析するだけで実現する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:332
msgid ""
"This is a difficult exercise. It will be solved in the solution, but it is "
"**not** necessary to complete it so as to proceed to the next step. I write "
"some hints here."
msgstr "難しい演習であり、解答では扱うが、次へ進むために終える必要は**ない**。ヒントを示す。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:334
msgid ""
"In solute tempering, the energy is a quadratic function of `sqrt(lambda)`. "
"In other words, for each frame, you could write the energy as "
"`A*lambda+B*sqrt(lambda)+C`, where `A`, `B`, and `C` are to be recomputed at"
" each frame. Analyze the `ene` array that we generated in the last exercise "
"so as to obtain these coefficients. The goal is to have a function that, for"
" any frame, and for any value of lambda (including values not yet "
"simulated!), returns the energy of the system."
msgstr ""
"Solute Tempering の Energy は `sqrt(lambda)` の2次関数である。各 Frame について "
"`A*lambda+B*sqrt(lambda)+C` と書け、`A`、`B`、`C` は Frame ごとに求める。前の演習の `ene` "
"を解析して係数を得る。目的は、まだ計算していない値を含む任意の lambda と、任意の Frame に対して Energy "
"を返す関数を作ることである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:339
msgid ""
"Using these functions, you will be able to compute weights corresponding to "
"arbitrary values of lambda. You could for instance use these weights to "
"generate a smooth version of the population vs lambda plot that we did in "
"the last exercise."
msgstr ""
"これらの関数により、任意の lambda に対応する Weight を求められる。例えば、前の Population と lambda "
"のグラフを滑らかな形で描ける。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:341
msgid ""
"Given two values of lambda, you can compute the average acceptance by doing "
"ensemble averages. You can easily test this function: use it to predict the "
"acceptance associated to the neighboring replicas simulated above. Can you "
"predict the acceptances seen during the simulation?"
msgstr ""
"2つの lambda の値があれば、Ensemble Averages で平均 Acceptance を計算できる。計算済みの隣接 Replicas の"
" Acceptance を予測し、実際の値と合うか確認してほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:345
msgid ""
"Once you have this function (let's call it "
"`predict_acceptance(lambda1,lambda2)`) you can use the following script to "
"find the ladder that maximizes the product of the acceptances. Let's say "
"that the largest lambda is fixed to 1.0 and the lowest is fixed to "
"`lambda_min`"
msgstr ""
"その関数を `predict_acceptance(lambda1,lambda2)` とすると、次のスクリプトで積を最大にする Ladder "
"を求められる。最大 lambda を1.0、最小を `lambda_min` に固定するとする。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:386
msgid ""
"You can then run a new simulation with the optimal lambdas and check if the "
"predicted acceptances correspond to the observed ones!"
msgstr "最適な lambda の組で新たに計算し、予測と観測の Acceptances が一致するかを確認してほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:389
msgid "Exercise 6: Combine with metadynamics on psi"
msgstr "演習6：psi の Metadynamics との組み合わせ"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:391
msgid ""
"As a very last point, repeat exercise the 5th exercise in [this "
"masterclass](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/masterclass-21-5.html) using alanine dipeptide in explicit solvent "
"and solute tempering with the lambda values optimized above. No further "
"guidance is provided for this exercise, but it should not be difficult "
"following the suggestions given in [this "
"masterclass](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/masterclass-21-5.html)."
msgstr ""
"最後に、明示的な溶媒中の Alanine Dipeptide、Solute Tempering、および最適化した lambda を使い、[こちらの "
"Masterclass](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/masterclass-21-5.html) "
"の演習5を繰り返す。追加の指針は示さないが、[こちら](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/masterclass-21-5.html)の提案を使えば難しくないはずである。"
